=
\frac{3V_{L}^{2}}{S_{base}}\] \[Z_{e}(base)_{\Delta}
=
\frac{3\times(11\times10^{3})^{2}}
{10^{5}}\] \[Z_{e}(base)_{\Delta}
=
3630\,\Omega\] Hence, \[Z_{e}(\Omega)
=
(0.02+j0.07)\times3630\] \[Z_{e}(\Omega)
=
(72.6+j254.1)\,\Omega\] \[\boxed{\text{D}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Per-unit impedance remains the same on both primary and secondary sides of a transformer.</li><li>Actual impedance can be obtained using: \[Z(\Omega)=Z(pu)\times Z(base)\]</li><li>Base impedance for a three-phase system: \[Z_{base}=\frac{3V_{L}^{2}}{S_{base}}\]</li></ul></div>

For a \(4\)-pole, \(50\,\text{Hz}\) induction motor, \[N_{s}=\frac{120f}{P}
=\frac{120\times 50}{4}
=1500\,\text{rpm}\] Rotor speed at full load is \[N_{r}=N_{s}(1-s)
=1500(1-0.04)
=1440\,\text{rpm}\] Given output power, \[P_{\text{out}}=15\,\text{kW}
=15000\,\text{W}\] Torque developed is \[T=\frac{P_{\text{out}}}{\omega_{r}}\] where \[\omega_{r}
=\frac{2\pi N_{r}}{60}
=\frac{2\pi \times 1440}{60}\] Hence, \[T
=\frac{15000}
{\dfrac{2\pi \times 1440}{60}}
=99.47\,\text{N}\cdot\text{m}\] \[\boxed{C}\]

For an \(8\)-pole, \(50\,\text{Hz}\) induction machine, the synchronous speed of the fundamental rotating magnetic field is \[N_{s}=\frac{120f}{P}
=\frac{120\times 50}{8}
=750\,\text{rpm}\] The synchronous speed of the \(n^{\text{th}}\) order space harmonic is \[N_{s,n}=\frac{N_{s}}{n}\] For the \(7^{\text{th}}\) space harmonic, \[N_{s,7}=\frac{750}{7}
=107.14\,\text{rpm}\] Also, harmonics of order \((3k+1)\) are positive-sequence harmonics and rotate in the forward direction, whereas harmonics of order \((3k-1)\) are negative-sequence harmonics and rotate in the reverse direction. Since \[7=3(2)+1\] the \(7^{\text{th}}\) harmonic is a positive-sequence harmonic and rotates in the forward direction. \[\boxed{A}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Fundamental synchronous speed: \(N_{s}=\dfrac{120f}{P}\).</li><li>Synchronous speed of \(n^{\text{th}}\) space harmonic: \(N_{s,n}=\dfrac{N_{s}}{n}\).</li><li>Harmonics of order \((3k+1)\) are positive-sequence (forward rotating).</li><li>Harmonics of order \((3k-1)\) are negative-sequence (backward rotating).</li></ul></div>

